From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: 2026-11-14
Subject: [PATCH] Keep plane snapshots: pre-deblock, pre-SAO, prediction, coefficients

Extends the DE265_INTERNALS build (patch 0001) with opt-in plane snapshots. A decoder context
with de265_internals_set_plane_snapshots(ctx, 1) gives every picture it starts afterwards
four extra planes per colour component, read with de265_internals_get_snapshot_plane():

  - PRE_DEBLOCK: the picture once every slice segment is decoded, before the in-loop filters,
  - PRE_SAO: the picture after deblocking, before SAO,
  - PREDICTION: the prediction of every transform block, taken in scale_coefficients() just
    before the residual is added in place; blocks without a residual take their
    reconstruction, PCM and cu_transquant_bypass coding units take 0 by convention,
  - COEFFICIENTS: int32 dequantised coefficients of every transform block at its sample
    positions.

The residual is PRE_DEBLOCK - PREDICTION and is not stored. The copies are taken at one point
for the sequential and the threaded filter paths (decctx.cc decode_some(), after the WPP/tile
tasks are waited for); with snapshots on, the threaded path lets deblocking finish before SAO
tasks start, which changes scheduling only. Snapshots are freed with the picture or by
de265_internals_release_snapshots() as soon as the consumer has copied them; with snapshots
off nothing is allocated and each hook is one pointer test. Decoded pictures are identical
with snapshots on and off.

All hooks have C linkage and the de265_internals_ prefix (de265_internals_hooks.h, not
installed), so the ON library still adds only de265_internals_* symbols; every change is
compiled only when DE265_INTERNALS is defined, so the OFF library stays identical to
upstream. Every modified upstream file carries a dated modification notice (GPL-3.0
section 5(a), through LGPL-3.0); the new header is LGPL-3.0-or-later like libde265.

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be offered to strukturag/libde265 after patch 0001, WI-2.167]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
Rationale: libde265 filters pictures in place and adds residuals into the prediction in place,
  so pre-filter planes, the prediction and the coefficients exist only transiently inside the
  decoder (chapter 07 section 7.6.2, patch 0003).
